``` MISP event 1 IOC hunts for Splunk.
    Indicators are simulated: fictional domain, RFC 5737 documentation IP, EICAR test-file hash.
    Run each search separately. Adjust index and sourcetype names to your environment.
    Searches 1 and 2 use the CIM Network_Resolution and Web data models. ```


``` ---- 1) DNS: hosts that resolved the phishing domain ---- ```
| tstats summariesonly=false count min(_time) as first_seen max(_time) as last_seen
    from datamodel=Network_Resolution.DNS
    where DNS.query="*secure-login-support.com"
    by DNS.src DNS.query
| convert ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)


``` ---- 2) Web / proxy: requests to the phishing domain or destination IP ---- ```
| tstats summariesonly=false count min(_time) as first_seen max(_time) as last_seen values(Web.url) as urls
    from datamodel=Web.Web
    where (Web.dest="*secure-login-support.com" OR Web.dest="198.51.100.23")
    by Web.src Web.user Web.dest
| eval reached_harvest_page=if(match(mvjoin(urls, " "), "/account/verify"), "yes", "no")
| convert ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)


``` ---- 3) Endpoint: attachment hash (EICAR) in Sysmon process creation ---- ```
index=* sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational" EventCode=1
    Hashes="*275A021BBFB6489E54D471899F7DB9D1663FC695EC2FE2A2C4538AABF651FD0F*"
| table _time host User Image Hashes ParentImage


``` ---- 4) All IOCs at once from a lookup ----
    Upload data/iocs.csv as lookup "misp_iocs.csv" after re-fanging it
    (replace [.] with . and hxxp with http), or export the event from MISP as CSV. ```
index=* (sourcetype=*dns* OR sourcetype=*proxy* OR sourcetype=*firewall*)
    [| inputlookup misp_iocs.csv | eval search="\"" . value . "\"" | fields search | format]
| stats count min(_time) as first_seen max(_time) as last_seen by host sourcetype
| convert ctime(first_seen) ctime(last_seen)
